From aaf3ab05e0b79f0df1b5e3624edef0304c7c7d74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:15:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Keep the mount root disjoint from source folders

Night Watch D4-01, G1-01/D4-02, D4-06, G5-04: a mount root equal to,
inside, or containing a source folder was accepted by set-mount-root,
source add, set-master-root and config-check (which even created it
inside the source), the scanner walked mount-root content as library
content, and `clean` / `doctor --repair clean_mount_root` removed the
user's empty source folders.

Add one shared, symlink-resolving disjointness rule
(ensure_mount_root_disjoint_from_sources; missing paths resolve through
their nearest existing ancestor) and apply it when setting the mount
root (all configured sources, enabled or not), adding a source, and
setting the master ROM root. config-check reports an overlapping config
as an error and no longer creates the mount root there. Cleanup
(plan_stale_mount_directories, clean_mount_root, cleanup_selected_mount_*)
fails closed on overlap, and the doctor repair refuses with a new
MountRootOverlapsSource rejection. The scanner excludes a mount root
inside a source, and live mounts when it is the source or contains it.

Regressions cover equal, child, parent, symlinked source, symlinked
mount root, a not-yet-created mount root, and disjoint controls. The
existing cleanup_selected_mount_* fixtures modelled the now-refused
"source inside mount root" layout; they now place the library beside
the mount root, keeping their boundary coverage.

