From 50de27ddd5fc567d2ecd282636c5aac14410d174 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:15:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Close the remaining mount-root overlap paths from review

Independent review of aaf3ab0 (F1-F4, F6, F8, F9):

- F1: the master ROM root is protected like a source: set_mount_root_to,
  config-check, every cleanup guard and the Doctor gates check it, and
  Doctor's source-root boundary includes it.
- F2 (partial): enabling a disabled source re-checks the mount root.
  Cleanup still sees enabled sources only (Config holds no others).
- F3: persisted catalogue scans exclude mount-root content and live
  mounts from a legacy overlapping source (arcade discovery included).
- F4: Doctor, create_configured_mount_root(_default), setup diagnostics'
  can_create_mount_root, mount-one/mount_unmounted_plan and batch
  validation refuse an overlapping mount root, so the refusal text is true.
- F6: a dangling symlink fails closed instead of being read as a missing
  folder. F9: set-master-root reports "cannot verify" truthfully.
- F8: Doctor tests assert MountRootOverlapsSource and run CleanMountPath
  on every listed folder; nine new regressions cover F1-F4, F6 and F9.

batch_validation_deduplicates_symlinked_parent_aliases_before_mounting
used a source containing its mount root; its library now sits beside
the mount root, keeping the alias coverage.

