From 3f2f9069295e4c4f0ac4f349fe2add16d1506cfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:07:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Protect disabled sources centrally and gate unknown
 source sets

Owner decision (round 3, option A): Config gains
`configured_source_roots: Option<Vec<PathBuf>>`, every configured source
path (enabled and disabled). parse_config, the only production loader,
always sets Some. ensure_mount_root_disjoint_from_config now checks
enabled sources, every configured source and the master ROM root, and
fails closed with a "cannot verify" error when the set is None. That one
guard covers clean, plan_stale_mount_directories, cleanup_selected_*, the
Doctor gates, Doctor mount-root creation, create_configured_mount_root,
batch validation and mount/mount-one/remount. Doctor's source-root
boundary also includes every configured source. Scan and read paths are
not gated.

Literals: the core-internal per-folder scan config, the GUI native-media
preview and core lib tests that never clean, mount or run Doctor use
None; every other literal uses Some(<its source_folders>).

C1: the native-media preview (and the bounded import built from it) now
scans with the configured mount root (new pub configured_mount_root_at),
so mount-root content inside the previewed source is excluded.

Regressions: a disabled [[source]] equal to, inside and containing the
mount root (loaded via Config::load_from) is refused by clean, the
stale plan, Doctor CleanMountRoot/CleanMountPath, run_doctor creation and
mount-one; disjoint disabled-source controls; a None set fails closed for
cleanup, creation and mount; the native-media preview skips mount-root
content.

